<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jungle Commando</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1986–1992</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Surinamese Liberation Army</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jungle Commando was a Maroon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> force led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ronnie-brunswijk">Ronnie Brunswijk</a> that fought the Surinamese National Army in the interior war of 1986 to 1992 against the military regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desi-bouterse">Desi Bouterse</a>. The fighting devastated Maroon villages in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, including Moiwana, and sent thousands of refugees into French Guiana. A peace accord in 1992 ended the conflict.</p></div>
